<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="55905" href="schedule/2010/fall/NRES/285/55905.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2010" href="schedule/2010.xml">2010</calendarYear><term id="120108" href="schedule/2010/fall.xml">Fall 2010</term><subject id="NRES" href="schedule/2010/fall/NRES.xml">Natural Resources and Environmental Sciences</subject><course id="285" href="schedule/2010/fall/NRES/285.xml">Field Experience</course></parents><sectionNumber>SP </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Field Exper. Suburban-Ponds</sectionTitle><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Stormwater drainage ponds are prominent features of suburban neighborhoods. Water quality, wildlife interactions, and people are all connected in these micro-ecosystems. Students will learn field techniques to assess homeowner perceptions and actions and to measure water quality (including impacts of wildlife and lawn care). Field work will be conducted in neighborhoods in southwest Champaign. This course meets Wednesdays, 1-1:50 lecture, 2-5 lab. Work will be required on 2-3 Saturdays (dates to be announced).</sectionText><sectionFeeAmount>ACES Field Trip $75.00 Flat Fee. </sectionFeeAmount><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2010-08-23Z</startDate><endDate>2010-12-08Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LBD">Laboratory-Discussion</type><start>01:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>S509</roomNumber><buildingName>Turner Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="David" firstName="M">David, M</instructor><instructor lastName="Flint" firstName="C">Flint, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>